derivations.claim:
Global identification. The tube of [F1] identifies a neighbourhood of $Z$ with a neighbourhood of the zero section of $
u_Z$. On each sufficiently small normal disk at $z\in Z$, the fibre component of $s$ has its only zero at $z$ and has invertible derivative there by [F6]. [[lem-choice-free-smooth-inverse-function-theorem-in-euclidean-space]] gives a local diffeomorphism. Its Jacobian is positive in the induced normal orientation, so using that diffeomorphism as an oriented coordinate chart identifies its pullback orientation generator with the positive source generator; over $\mathbb F_2$ the degree is $1$ regardless of sign. Thus step 1.2 says precisely that the relative pullback restricts to the prescribed generator on every normal fibre pair. Thom uniqueness [F3] identifies it on the tube with $u_{
u_Z}$. Excision [F4] identifies $H^r(M,M\setminus Z;R)$ with the relative cohomology of that tube and its complement of $Z$; radial deformation in each fibre identifies the latter with $H^r(D(
u_Z),S(
u_Z);R)$. Hence $s^*(u_E)$ is the image of $u_{
u_Z}$ under the tubular identification.

